<BaseLayout title="CV17 (Shanzhong) — Chest Center Point" description="Learn how to locate and stimulate CV17 (Shanzhong) — the Chest Center point on the sternum. Benefits include breathing support, asthma relief, and emotional release." breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Points", href: "/points" }, { label: "CV17 (Shanzhong)", href: "/points/cv17-shanzhong-acupressure-point" }]} articleSchema={true}>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 lg:px-6">
    <h1 class="mb-4">CV17 (Shanzhong) — Chest Center</h1>
    <p class="text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400 text-lg mb-8">CV17, known as Shanzhong or Chest Center, is the front Mu point of the Pericardium. It is used for breathing difficulties, chest tightness, and emotional release.</p>

    <section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Location</h2>
    <img src="/images/cv17-location.webp" alt="CV17 acupressure point location on the center of the chest" class="w-full max-w-sm mx-auto rounded-xl shadow-sm" />
    <p class="mb-3">CV17 is located on the midline of the sternum (breastbone), at the level of the fourth intercostal space, approximately at nipple height in most people.</p>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Benefits &amp; Uses</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-3 space-y-1 text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      <li><strong>Breathing support:</strong> CV17 relieves chest tightness, shortness of breath, and asthma symptoms.</li>
      <li><strong>Emotional release:</strong> It is the point for releasing grief, sadness, and suppressed emotions stored in the chest.</li>
      <li><strong>Anxiety and stress:</strong> CV17 calms the heart and mind, reducing anxiety and panic sensations.</li>
      <li><strong>Heart health:</strong> It helps with palpitations, chest pain, and general heart Qi discomfort.</li>
      <li><strong>Hiccups and cough:</strong> CV17 can help stop persistent hiccups and soothe dry or spasmodic coughs.</li>
    </ul>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">How to Massage CV17</h2>
    <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2 text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      <li>Lie down or sit comfortably with your chest exposed.</li>
      <li>Place two or three fingertips of one hand on the CV17 point.</li>
      <li>Apply gentle to moderate pressure in a small circular motion.</li>
      <li>Breathe deeply for 1— minutes while maintaining contact.</li>
      <li>Use a palm rub in a clockwise motion over the sternum to finish.</li>
    </ol>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Science &amp; Research</h2>
    <p class="mb-3">A 2021 study in <em>Medicine</em> found that CV17 acupressure improved pulmonary function and reduced dyspnea in patients with COPD.<sup><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34596136/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">1</a></sup> Research in <em>Journal of Alternative and Complementary Medicine</em> showed that CV17 stimulation reduced anxiety and improved heart rate variability, indicating better autonomic balance.<sup><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31343261/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">2</a></sup></p>
    <p class="mb-3">A 2020 review in <em>Evidence-Based Complementary and Alternative Medicine</em> highlighted CV17 as the most commonly used acupoint for treating emotional disorders, particularly grief and depression.<sup><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32655759/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">3</a></sup></p>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Precautions</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-3 space-y-1 text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      <li>Use gentle pressure on the sternum ?the bone is sensitive and excessive force can cause bruising.</li>
      <li>Avoid if you have a recent chest injury, rib fracture, or chest surgery.</li>
      <li>Do not apply pressure if you have skin conditions, rashes, or burns on the chest.</li>
      <li>Consult a healthcare provider if you have a known heart condition before using this point.</li>
    </ul>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Related Points</h2>
    <p class="mb-3">CV17 pairs well with <a href="/points/pc6-neiguan-acupressure-point">PC6 (Neiguan)</a> for chest tightness and anxiety. For emotional release, combine with <a href="/points/lv3-taichong-acupressure-point">LV3 (Taichong)</a> and <a href="/points/cv6-qihai-acupressure-point">CV6 (Qihai)</a>.</p>
  </section></article>
</BaseLayout>
